{{About|the dead body left after a creature has been killed}}

Most creatures leave corpses on the ground when [[kill]]ed. [[Totem]]s, [[frozen|shattered]] monsters, and enemies destroyed by certain effects cannot leave corpses.

==Mechanics==
Various mechanics interact with corpses. For example: 
* Corpses may be created (e.g. {{il|Desecrate}}, {{il|Unearth}}, {{il|Corpsewalker}}) 
** Different skills have individual maximum corpse limits. 
** Spawning corpses technically spawns living monsters and then kills them.<ref>https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/1676002/filter-account-type/staff/page/5#p16228730</ref> This does not normally credit the player in any way, but it may contribute to quest progression.<ref>https://www.reddit.com/r/pathofexile/comments/18kpl2x/find_and_defeat_500_nameless_creatures_cheese/</ref> 
* Corpses may be required for effects (e.g. {{il|Raise Spectre}}, {{il|General's Cry}}, {{il|Detonate Dead}}, {{il|Spirit Offering}}), often consuming them. 
* Corpses may be consumed on kill (e.g. {{il|Void Sphere}}, {{il|Absolution}}).
* Corpses may be prevented by on-kill destruction or explosions (e.g. {{il|Pyre}}, {{il|Infernal Blow}}, {{psl|Profane Bloom}}).  
** Despite destroying enemies, these effects do not interfere with on-kill corpse consumption like {{il|Dominating Blow}} or {{il|Voltaxic Burst}}. They do prevent consumption by {{il|Void Sphere}}. 

Any mechanic that actively removes an existing corpse counts as '''consuming''' it.<ref>https://discord.com/channels/174993814845521922/174994219390337024/722918172369616936</ref> This does not include removing corpses by spawning more than a skill's maximum. Removing corpses can be useful to prevent certain on-death effects, or enemy interactions with corpses, such as [[Necromancer (monster type)|Necromancer]] monsters, [[strongbox]]es with the {{Ml|ChestExplodeCorpses}} prefix, or the "Explodes Corpses" [[monster modifier]]. 

Corpses can be targeted by holding the {{key press|A}} key by default (PC), but only if the player has a skill that can target corpses.

The amount of maximum life of the corpse scales with the area's level, capped at level 83 (same as tier 16 maps). Player-spawned corpses are not affected by the map's modifiers.

===Spectral Corpse===
If a player has access to the regular {{il|Raise Spectre}} skill and has at least 1 monster saved in the [[spectre bank]], using {{il|Desecrate}} or {{sl|Corpse Walk}} has a 15% chance to spawn as a Spectral Corpse instead of a random area monster corpse (or 100% in [[hideout]]s). The corpses can only be interacted with through [[minion]] skills, and cannot be otherwise detonated or consumed. Spectral Corpses have a visual effect applied to them to help differentiate them from other corpses.

[[Corpse item]]s also create a Spectral Corpse on use.

The following skills can be used on Spectral Corpses:

* {{il|Raise Zombie}}
** {{il|Raise Zombie of Slamming}}
* {{il|Raise Spectre}}
** {{il|Raise Spectre of Transience}}
* {{il|Dominating Blow}}
** {{il|Dominating Blow of Inspiring}}
* {{il|Bone Offering}}
* {{il|Flesh Offering}}
* {{il|Spirit Offering}}
* {{sl|Blood Offering}}

